  "Attributes": [
    {
      "Id": 960206,
      "attributeType": "LongString",
      "attributeName": "AIDescription",
      "attributeRelationType": "None",
      "Value": "## 10 Years for Commodore 64: A Synopsis\n\nTen years have passed since Winston Smith’s rebellion in Oceania. The Party’s grip remains absolute, but cracks are beginning to appear. *10 Years for Commodore 64* plunges you into this oppressive world as a new protagonist, a young technician named Elias, who discovers a hidden cache of pre-Party data – a dangerous spark of hope in a society built on manufactured ignorance.\n\nThis retro-inspired platformer delivers a chilling narrative experience, blending Orwellian themes with classic 8-bit gameplay. Navigate treacherous environments, evade omnipresent surveillance drones, and confront the chilling reality of a world where thoughtcrime is the ultimate transgression. \n\nElias must use his technical skills to decipher the data, uncover the truth about the past, and potentially ignite a new flame of resistance. Expect challenging platforming sequences, limited resources, and a constant sense of paranoia as you evade the watchful eyes of Big Brother. Can you expose the Party’s lies and offer a glimmer of hope to a broken nation?"
    },
